summary: Setup bare metal Kernel for Kdump.
description: |
    It setups main kernel and kdump kernel parameters and installs necessary Kdump and debuginfo packages for later exercise of Kdump and crash-utility.

    Accepted Parameters
    - KER1ARGS: a series of additional main kernel boot parameters separated by
      white spaces.
      E.g. 'crashkernel=64M@16M intel_iommu=on'

    - NODEBUGINFO: Whether to intall kernel-debuginfo which is required for testing Crash utilities. Setting it to true means it will not install kernel-debuginfo and kernel-debuginfo-common packages. By default, it's true.
      E.g. NODEBUGINFO=true

contact: Kdump QE <kdump-qe-list@redhat.com>
test: make run
framework: shell
duration: 30m
extra-summary: /kernel/kdump/setup-bare-metal
extra-task: /kernel/kdump/setup-bare-metal

require:
  - kexec-tools
  - make
  - type: file
    pattern:
      - /cmdline_helper
      - /cki_lib
      - /kdump/include
      - /automotive/include
recommend: 
  - wget
  - abootimg

adjust:
    - when: NODEBUGINFO==true
      recommend+: 
        - kernel-debuginfo 
